//
// A LINK TO AN UNDECLARED GROUP IS REFUSED (`@FR-Cap-Deny`, `@FR-Cap-Write`).  Groups are declared
// (`capability g`), and a `group#right` link naming one that is not — here the misspelt `helth`
// beside the declared `health` — is a load error, whatever the profile grants.  The diagnostic
// carries no source position, so it is claimed file-wide; the write the misspelt link guards is
// refused beside it (`helth#update` is granted by no profile), and that refusal is claimed too.
//
// @falsified-at: none — a conformance guard: the refusal held on the tree it landed on.  (Its first
//   draft read the runner as dropping the refusal; it was consumed by the claim while the WRITE
//   refusal beside it went unclaimed.)
// CHANNEL: the expected diagnostic (an admission refusal at load).
// ARMED: the `[sandbox]` policy in this directory's loft.toml.
// WITNESS: the refusal names the undeclared group.
// HOLDS: `loft --interpret` and `sandbox-check` refuse the file the same way.
// @EXPECT_ERROR: undeclared capability `helth` — a `group#right` link references it but no matching `capability` is declared
// @EXPECT_ERROR: sandboxed `deny_undeclared` writes host field `hp`, which needs capability `helth#update`

capability health

struct Typo { hp: integer helth#update }

fn deny_undeclared(t: Typo) { t.hp = 0; }
